As part of the government&#39;s Anti-Crisis Shield, a number of solutions have been introduced to support businesses. Among the instruments introduced are:
· non-repayable loan for companies that maintain permanent employment from the Labor Fund - micro-companies that employ no more than 9 employees can receive a loan of PLN 5,000;
· automatic working capital loan;
· extension of the BGK de minimis guarantee program for SMEs;
· possibility of settling the loss incurred in 2020 from the income obtained in 2019;
· exemption from ZUS contributions for micro-entrepreneurs, but also for the self-employed for a period of 3 months;
· &quot;New Chance Policy&quot; programme for SMEs;
· more favorable conditions for the Loan for technological innovations;
· Financial Shield 1.0 and 2.0 of the Polish Development Fund. The government plans to allocate approximately PLN 30 billion to help entrepreneurs affected by the COVID-19 pandemic and protect jobs in the second quarter of 2021. The most important elements of support include: expanding the list industries that can apply for support (over 60 industries in total), assistance in rent regulation for tenants, 100% cancellation of subsidies from the PFR Financial Shield 1.0, co-financing of disinfection agents for restaurants, fitness clubs and hotels.

